-- title:
--   Equality with a finite flat closed subscheme is a closed condition
-- statement:
--   Let $Z$, $D$, $T$ be schemes (in a fixed universe), let $i : Z \to D$ be a closed immersion, and let $g : D \to T$ be finite, flat and locally of finite presentation. The assertion is that there is an ideal sheaf datum $J$ on $T$ — that is, a quasi-coherent ideal sheaf of $\mathcal{O}_T$, equivalently a closed subscheme of $T$ — with the following universal property: for every scheme $T'$ and every morphism $h : T' \to T$, the inverse image ideal sheaf $J \cdot \mathcal{O}_{T'}$ vanishes if and only if the inverse image of the kernel ideal sheaf $\ker(\mathcal{O}_D \to i_*\mathcal{O}_Z)$ along the first projection $D \times_T T' \to D$ of the fibre product of $g$ and $h$ vanishes. In other words, the closed subscheme of $T$ cut out by $J$ represents, on all $T$-schemes and not merely on points, the condition that the base change of the closed immersion $i$ to $T'$ be an isomorphism, i.e. that the closed subscheme $Z \times_T T'$ of $D \times_T T'$ be the whole of $D \times_T T'$. No uniqueness of $J$ is asserted.
--
--   This is the form taken by the lemma of Katz–Mazur (Arithmetic Moduli of Elliptic Curves, 1.3.4) that equality of a closed subscheme with an ambient scheme finite flat over the base is a closed condition on the base, stated here as the representability of that condition by a closed subscheme of $T$. It is used in the construction of the closed subscheme of the base over which a family of points forms a Drinfeld basis, via [`WeierstrassProjModel.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_idealSheafData_comap_eq_bot_iff_isDrinfeldBasisOver`](thm.html#WeierstrassProjModel.RelativeGroupLaw.exists_idealSheafData_comap_eq_bot_iff_isDrinfeldBasisOver), where the two inclusions between the subgroup generated by the points and the torsion subscheme are each of this shape.
